{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960696,"nonce":"AjOOM9BwddgfpFMuGRFBtTB7Yc0=","title":"native primitives' signatures are never checked","message":"`native_lib.rs` asks each `hlp_*` resolver for its signature (`let mut sign = null; resolver(\u0026mut sign)`) and discards it. Stock HashLink compares the signature with the call's types and refuses a mismatch (src/module.c, \"Invalid signature for function\"). docs/hdll.md says Ash checks it too.\n\nWithout the check a mismatched primitive runs with the wrong layout. x-idl's HashLink target read every `haxe.io.Bytes` as a `String` (x-idl c980074d4d6e099e136fcc82e634a4afe09bda2e76120d68f850ee909f02189e, fixed): stock HashLink would have refused `OBi_` for a Bytes argument, while under Ash the copy wrote two bytes to a wild address and the program carried on.","files":null}]}